1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,407
A website search needs four parts:

2
00:00:03,407 --> 00:00:08,582
an index, a setting that picks it, a permission to query it, and a results page.

3
00:00:08,582 --> 00:00:13,155
This video builds all four with Lucene, then tunes what is indexed and

4
00:00:13,155 --> 00:00:14,780
how the results look.

5
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:24,329
A content item produces a full-text value from its display text, its body,

6
00:00:24,329 --> 00:00:26,123
and any Liquid you add.

7
00:00:26,123 --> 00:00:32,680
The indexer stores that value in the Content.ContentItem.FullText field of an index that you create.

8
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:36,526
The Search feature adds the search page at /search.

9
00:00:36,526 --> 00:00:40,872
It matches a visitor's terms against the index you choose in the settings,

10
00:00:40,872 --> 00:00:45,000
checks a permission for that index, and draws the results with shapes.

11
00:00:49,232 --> 00:00:50,833
Open Tools, Features.

12
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:56,050
Lucene creates and queries the indexes, and Search adds the front-end search page.

13
00:00:56,050 --> 00:01:00,082
Let's type Lucene in the search box to find the first feature.

14
00:01:00,546 --> 00:01:02,794
Select Enable on the Lucene feature.

15
00:01:02,794 --> 00:01:05,686
A message confirms that the feature was enabled.

16
00:01:06,153 --> 00:01:09,148
Then search for Search, and enable the Search feature.

17
00:01:09,148 --> 00:01:13,043
It brings the Site Search settings and the search page of the front end.

18
00:01:17,273 --> 00:01:20,220
Under Search, Indexes, select Add index.

19
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:24,128
The Available Sources dialog lists what can be indexed.

20
00:01:24,128 --> 00:01:26,563
Select Add on Content in Lucene.

21
00:01:27,027 --> 00:01:31,029
Type Posts as the Index Name, the name of the index in Lucene.

22
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:33,324
The Name field fills in as posts.

23
00:01:33,324 --> 00:01:37,327
The search page address and the permission both use that name.

24
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:42,910
Content types lists the content types of the site, and at least one is required.

25
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,640
Let's select Blog Post.

26
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:51,407
The Analyzer controls how Lucene prepares text for the index, and standardanalyzer is the default.

27
00:01:51,407 --> 00:01:56,984
Store Source Data, which keeps field values in the index for retrieval, stays cleared.

28
00:01:57,435 --> 00:02:03,254
Under Default Query Settings, Query field names lists the fields of the index.

29
00:02:03,254 --> 00:02:10,875
Only Content.ContentItem.FullText is selected, so a search matches the full-text value and nothing else.

30
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:12,375
Select Save.

31
00:02:12,375 --> 00:02:17,818
A message says that the index was created and that synchronizing runs in the background.

32
00:02:17,818 --> 00:02:21,003
The list shows posts with Lucene as its provider.

33
00:02:22,603 --> 00:02:27,655
The built-in analyzer is registered with the Lucene options in a Startup class.

34
00:02:27,655 --> 00:02:31,221
A module adds its own the same way, with a name and an

35
00:02:31,221 --> 00:02:35,203
analyzer instance, and the name appears in the Analyzer list.

36
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:41,953
Open Settings, Search, Site Search.

37
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:45,433
Default search index lists the indexes of the site.

38
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:46,960
Let's select posts.

39
00:02:47,516 --> 00:02:51,040
Placeholder is the text shown in the empty search box.

40
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,566
Type a short prompt, and select Save.

41
00:02:57,759 --> 00:03:01,045
The search page checks a permission for the index.

42
00:03:01,045 --> 00:03:05,269
Open Access Control, Roles, and select Edit on the Anonymous role.

43
00:03:05,735 --> 00:03:08,600
In the Search permissions box, type posts.

44
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:13,732
Check Allow on Query 'posts' Index, which lets the search page query this index.

45
00:03:13,732 --> 00:03:18,985
Query Lucene Posts Index is listed as well, but the search page does not check it.

46
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:20,448
Select Save.

47
00:03:20,448 --> 00:03:24,990
Visitors who are not signed in can query this index through the search page.

48
00:03:29,206 --> 00:03:30,999
Open /search on the site.

49
00:03:30,999 --> 00:03:35,856
The theme draws the form, and the box shows the placeholder from the settings.

50
00:03:36,314 --> 00:03:38,280
Type apple, and select Search.

51
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:42,648
The page lists the posts whose full-text value contains the word, each one

52
00:03:42,648 --> 00:03:46,034
drawn with the Summary display type of its content type.

53
00:03:46,491 --> 00:03:49,566
Grafting appears only in the subtitle of a post.

54
00:03:49,566 --> 00:03:54,066
Searching for it shows There are no such results, because the subtitle is

55
00:03:54,066 --> 00:03:56,231
not part of the full-text value.

56
00:04:00,431 --> 00:04:05,255
The Full-text section of a content type editor controls its full-text value.

57
00:04:05,255 --> 00:04:10,080
Include display text and Include body parts are selected by default, and Use

58
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,611
custom full-text adds the output of a Liquid template.

59
00:04:15,199 --> 00:04:20,077
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and select Edit on Blog Post.

60
00:04:20,077 --> 00:04:23,839
The Full-text section sits among the settings of the type.

61
00:04:24,301 --> 00:04:26,214
Select Use custom full-text.

62
00:04:26,214 --> 00:04:30,717
In the editor that opens, type a Liquid expression that reads the Subtitle

63
00:04:30,717 --> 00:04:32,631
field of the Blog Post part.

64
00:04:33,085 --> 00:04:34,109
Select Save.

65
00:04:34,109 --> 00:04:38,547
Items that are already indexed keep their old value until they are saved

66
00:04:38,547 --> 00:04:40,595
again or the index is rebuilt.

67
00:04:42,195 --> 00:04:45,511
To index widgets too, use the full_text filter.

68
00:04:45,511 --> 00:04:49,953
It returns the full-text value of each content item in a list, so

69
00:04:49,953 --> 00:04:54,145
the second line adds the text of every widget in a Flow part.

70
00:04:58,355 --> 00:05:03,782
Under Search, Indexes, open the Actions menu of posts and select Rebuild, which

71
00:05:03,782 --> 00:05:06,655
removes the index and creates it again.

72
00:05:07,125 --> 00:05:12,115
A message says that the index was rebuilt and that synchronizing runs in the background.

73
00:05:12,578 --> 00:05:14,317
Search for grafting again.

74
00:05:14,317 --> 00:05:18,771
The post whose subtitle contains the word is listed, because the subtitle is

75
00:05:18,771 --> 00:05:20,618
part of the full-text value.

76
00:05:24,818 --> 00:05:27,227
Three shapes build the search page.

77
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:34,453
Search-List arranges the page, Search-Form draws the search box, and Search-Results draws the matching content items.

78
00:05:34,453 --> 00:05:38,448
A theme overrides one by adding a template with the same name.

79
00:05:39,198 --> 00:05:42,449
Search-Results draws each item with a display type.

80
00:05:42,449 --> 00:05:47,809
Change Summary to SearchSummary, then add a SearchSummary template for each content type

81
00:05:47,809 --> 00:05:49,348
that the index holds.

82
00:05:53,548 --> 00:05:56,577
A recipe repeats the setup on another site.

83
00:05:56,577 --> 00:06:02,944
The feature step enables Search and Lucene, and CreateOrUpdateIndexProfile creates the index with

84
00:06:02,944 --> 00:06:05,478
its content types and query fields.

85
00:06:06,228 --> 00:06:11,096
The Settings step selects the index for the search page, RebuildIndex fills it,

86
00:06:11,096 --> 00:06:14,533
and the Roles step grants the permission to Anonymous.

87
00:06:14,533 --> 00:06:18,828
TheBlogTheme includes these steps as the Blog - Lucene Search recipe.

88
00:06:20,828 --> 00:06:24,948
An index, the Site Search settings, a permission, and a results page make

89
00:06:24,948 --> 00:06:29,120
a full-text search, and the full-text value and the templates tune what is

90
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,632
found and how it looks.

91
00:06:30,632 --> 00:06:31,988
Thanks for watching.

